{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::execute` receives a context for its\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node` and computes its\ncompleted answer:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse std::future::Future;\n\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Select inputs through cx and compute the completed answer.\n    fn execute(\n        self,\n        cx: &mut ValidationContext<'_, D>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Self::Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nAn `Ok` value is the answer defined by\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait.answer`.\nAn `Err` value reports a [validation error](running-criteria.md#habeas-req-requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.ValidationError).",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately cover `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.execute`. I judged this from the supplied test sources and did not request any implementation source.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. `execute` receives a context for the criterion's source node.\n2. On success it computes the completed answer, and that answer is the `Ok` value.\n3. A failure is returned as `Err`, a `ValidationError`.\n4. The returned future is `Send`. The `self` and `&mut ValidationContext` signature is part of the contract.\n\n**Mapping obligations to tests**\n- **Context bound to the source node, and `Ok` carries the answer.**\n  - `criterion_decode_errors_are_execution_errors_and_false_is_a_completed_answer` (`validation_tests.rs`) defines a criterion whose `execute` reads `cx.node_id()`. The result carries the dependency `Dependency::Node(node 1, fp(\"false\"))`, so the context was bound to the source node. The test also asserts that a negative answer (`false`) is a completed `Ok`, and that the stored output is `json!(false)`.\n  - `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent` (`agent/tests.rs`) checks the computed output (`result` and `rationale`) and the node dependency recorded from the source-node read.\n  - `domain_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk` (`src/authoring/sdk.rs`) checks that the `Ok` answer has the expected determination and rationale and that it is persisted. It also checks that the stored record equals the answer.\n  - `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` checks the successful agent-backed result and its dependencies.\n- **`Err` reports a validation error.** The tests cover these cases:\n  - Output decode failure: `ValidationError::Output` in the decode test.\n  - Missing agent: `NoAgentConfigured` in the `deterministic_validation…` and `runner_does_not_store…` tests.\n  - Invalid agent submission: `ValidationError::Agent` in `invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error`.\n  - Graph errors raised inside the callback: `ValidationError::Graph` in `resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments`.\n  - The `Agent` variant payload: `agent_errors_expose_the_agreed_string_payload`.\n  - Failed executions store no record, which the tests assert.\n- **`Send` future and signature.** `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` (`tests/contracts.rs`) passes the verify and store futures through a `send(...)` bound helper. It asserts the output and that execution ran once. The test criteria implement `execute` with the required `self` and `&mut ValidationContext` signature.\n\n**Delegated obligations**\nThe serde round-trip of `Ok` belongs to the cited `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait.answer`. `contracts.rs` also tests that requirement, and it is cited context here.\n\nI found no plausible requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
